  "section_notes": "S1 requires all thermal incidents to be reported within 72 hours, with 7-day customer notice, but does not explicitly require reporting during investigation. S2 keeps the 5% limit and customer-facing numeric results, but allows open-ended sale above 5% if the regulator authorizes, weakening the cap. S3 mandates new-unit shut-off and a 6-year retrofit, but includes a 'where technically feasible' escape with no alternative. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 sets an 8/100k notification trigger but makes recall conditional on regulator determination with open-ended corrective action."
